WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:09.085
Plain text goes to the leader of the project at hand.

2
00:00:09.085 --> 00:00:15.553
It reads the checkout, splits your request into cards and posts them on the board;

3
00:00:15.553 --> 00:00:17.289
the workers take them.

4
00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:21.075
Its reply comes back as an item waiting for you.

5
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:24.616
At-name writes to one agent.

6
00:00:24.616 --> 00:00:30.470
After the at sign, tab completes the names, the project at hand first.

7
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.738
A message to an idle worker opens a card; its answer closes it.

8
00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:42.345
A line that starts with a slash is the agent's own command line: slash compact,

9
00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:45.606
slash cost, whatever Claude Code knows.

10
00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:52.036
v opens your conversation with the agent at hand, here the leader.

11
00:00:52.036 --> 00:00:58.058
Every message on the bus has a number, and a reply names the one it answers.

12
00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:04.397
Capital J opens the journal; enter on one of its lines opens the conversation it

13
00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.268
belongs to.

14
00:01:05.268 --> 00:01:11.607
A reply is marked with an arrow, and the percent key goes to what it answers and

15
00:01:11.607 --> 00:01:12.003
back.

16
00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:18.658
The brackets go from turn to turn: the lines one side says before the other answers.

17
00:01:26.201 --> 00:01:33.312
Hash opens the card line with the card at hand already in it; a number or a word of

18
00:01:33.312 --> 00:01:35.197
a title names another.

19
00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:42.393
Enter opens its detail: who works on it, its story, the lines about it; tab turns to

20
00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:45.306
its owner's diff and conversation.

21
00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:49.332
n and p step to the next and the previous card.

22
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:54.691
Every key that acts has a colon name too.

23
00:01:54.691 --> 00:02:03.109
Colon and tab show the commands with what each stands at now: the theme, the budget

24
00:02:03.109 --> 00:02:08.281
spent and left, the project a bare command acts on.

25
00:02:08.281 --> 00:02:13.758
A dollar sign marks the ones that raise the next bill.

26
00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:18.424
Colon budget changes the pot while agents run.

27
00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:26.002
Colon theme wears each theme while its name is written: the built-in ones, base16

28
00:02:26.002 --> 00:02:30.489
schemes, or a colour file in Ghostty's or Kitty's format.

29
00:02:30.489 --> 00:02:33.245
Enter keeps it, escape gives it up.

30
00:02:33.245 --> 00:02:38.756
The terminal theme follows your terminal's own colours, light or dark.

31
00:02:39.956 --> 00:02:43.954
Capital L turns the screen Turkish, and back.

32
00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:51.061
Every word on the screen lives in both languages; what an agent wrote is cleaned

33
00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:58.168
before it is drawn, control characters removed and secret-looking tokens hidden.

34
00:02:59.368 --> 00:03:05.905
Question mark lists the keys of the screen you are on; again, every key.

35
00:03:05.905 --> 00:03:13.441
Slash finds any key by every word you type, Turkish letters or not; enter keeps the

36
00:03:13.441 --> 00:03:15.620
filter, escape drops it.

37
00:03:19.543 --> 00:03:25.946
h and l fold a project to its heading; a folded project is one line that still shows

38
00:03:25.946 --> 00:03:26.785
what waits.

39
00:03:26.785 --> 00:03:32.808
The brackets narrow Home to one project, then the next, then all of them again.

40
00:03:32.808 --> 00:03:38.754
Colon open adds another checkout as a project of its own, with its own leader.

41
00:03:46.413 --> 00:03:50.905
One line to the leader, and a key for everything else.

